<title>ITALY: Italian CPI 3.4 pct in August - Istat.</title>
<headline>Italian CPI 3.4 pct in August - Istat.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Office (ISTAT) reported the following consumer inflation details:</p>
<p> ITALIAN INFLATION	   AUG 96    JULY 96   (AUG 95)</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index rise	 0.1	 -0.2	(0.3)</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     3.4	  3.6	(5.8)</p>
<p> Index (Base 1996)	    104.1	104.0    (114.9)</p>
<p>Note: The 1996 data is based on a new basket of goods. The 1995 data was collated under an old basket.</p>
<p>Istat said that including tobacco costs in the inflation data gave a CPI rate of 3.5 percent for August.</p>
<p>ISTAT gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown.</p>
<p> Sector			   Index	   mo/mo (%)    yr/yr (%)</p>
<p> Food (without tabacco)     104.9	   -0.2	   +4.3</p>
<p> Clothing			 104.3	    0.0	   +4.3</p>
<p> Housing,Electricity,Fuel   104.1	   +0.6	   +3.6</p>
<p> Domestic goods		 104.1	   +0.2	   +3.2</p>
<p> Health spending		102.5	    0.0	   +2.3</p>
<p> Transport			105.2	   +0.3	   +3.8</p>
<p> Recreation		     102.5	   +0.2	   +1.9</p>
<p> Education			104.1	   +0.1	   +4.4</p>
<p> Hotels, restaurants	  104.5	   +0.1	   +3.9</p>
<p>Other goods,services</p>
<p> (including communications) 103.1	    0.0	   +1.9</p>
</text>
